parts.text:
Guardian layout has no theme handling at all (interesting — the guardian portal probably stays light, but that's a separate concern; the `.dark` class on html affects it though). The `dark` class is set on `document.documentElement` globally, so guardian pages would also render dark — but guardian layout components use their own light styles... not my current concern.

For the accent color fix, the scope: main-layout (app shell) is the primary place. I'll create the helper and:
1. `src/app/core/utils/theme.ts`: `applyAccentColor(color)` — sets `--primary`, `--primary-rgb`, `--primary-dark`, `--primary-light`.
2. Configurações: use helper in setAccentColor + ngOnInit.
3. Main-layout ngOnInit: apply saved accent.

For darken/lighten: simple hex manipulation. Primary default #007F80 (teal). If user picks #6366f1 (indigo), dark = multiply by ~0.8, light = blend with white ~ 85%.

Let me write the utility:

```ts
export function hexToRgb(hex: string): string {
  const h = hex.replace('#', '');
  const full = h.length === 3 ? h.split('').map(c => c + c).join('') : h;
  const n = parseInt(full, 16);
  return `${(n >> 16) & 255}, ${(n >> 8) & 255}, ${n & 255}`;
}

export function shadeHex(hex: string, factor: number): string {
  const h = hex.replace('#', '');
  const full = h.length === 3 ? h.split('').map(c => c + c).join('') : h;
  const n = parseInt(full, 16);
  const r = Math.round(((n >> 16) & 255) * factor);
  const g = Math.round(((n >> 8) & 255) * factor);
  const b = Math.round((n & 255) * factor);
  return `#${((r << 16) | (g << 8) | b).toString(16).padStart(6, '0')}`;
}

export function applyAccentColor(color: string) {
  const el = document.documentElement;
  el.style.setProperty('--primary', color);
  el.style.setProperty('--primary-rgb', hexToRgb(color));
  el.style.setProperty('--primary-dark', shadeHex(color, 0.8));
  el.style.setProperty('--primary-light', mixHex(color, '#ffffff', 0.85)); // light tint
}
```

--primary-light in light mode is used for subtle backgrounds (e.g., `bg-primary-light`?) — from styles: `--primary-light: #E0F5F5` — a very light tint of teal. To approximate for arbitrary color: blend with white at ~88%. Let me add a mix function.

Check what uses --primary-light: grep showed only definition. `bg-primary-light` might be used in tailwind config — tailwind colors reference CSS vars? The app uses `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `ring-primary` etc. as Tailwind classes — these come from a Tailwind config theme extension. Let me check tailwind.config to see if primary maps to `var(--primary)` — that would confirm that setting `--primary` on :root actually changes all Tailwind primary utilities.

